2026-08-25T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Running the ported converter on real geometry, 2026-09-12: the Dress's
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-1029) '6,408 triangles pair into 3,204 quads with NOTHING left over, 100.0%
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-1029) 'coverage. Dress_shoulder reaches 99.4% and Dress_Ribbon 95.3%.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-1029) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-1029) 'A perfect pairing does not happen by luck. It means the mesh was authored
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-1029) 'as quads and triangulated on export, so the original edge flow is intact
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-1029) 'and recoverable. That is the same property RFD66606-2029 wants from a curvenet:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-1029) 'a bounded, inspectable graph rather than a soup.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-1029) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-1029) '**Recovering quads does not by itself save a triangle.** The platform counts
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-1029) 'triangles and a quad is two of them, so 6,408 in is 6,408 out. The value is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-1029) 'that a quad mesh with intact flow supports removing a whole edge loop, which
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-1029) 'halves resolution in one direction and preserves the flow, where quadric
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-1029) 'decimation picks vertices by error and leaves flow to chance. On a garment,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-1029) 'whose silhouette IS its edge flow, that difference is the point.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-1029) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-1029) 'The curvenet idea applies in this adapted form rather than directly. CASSIE
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-1029) 'authors a curve network from strokes; it does not reverse-engineer one from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-1029) 'a dense mesh, and the capability inventory records its patch surface
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-1029) 'creation as losing about 90%. For an existing mesh the practical form of the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-1029) 'same idea is field-guided retopology at a chosen budget, which Instant
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-1029) 'Meshes already provides under BSD-3.
 # tags: rfd:details
