 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:19Z (RFD66606-1029) 'So the meshes whose shapes cover them can be left alone. Those are the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:20Z (RFD66606-1029) 'face tracking meshes, where a shape moving four vertices is exactly
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:21Z (RFD66606-1029) 'what decimation removes first.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:22Z (RFD66606-1029) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:23Z (RFD66606-1029) 'If a transfer is ever needed, the trap is recorded here. A shape that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:24Z (RFD66606-1029) 'moves four vertices is invisible in any rest-pose comparison, because
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:25Z (RFD66606-1029) 'at weight zero the mesh is correct. Verification has to evaluate each
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:26Z (RFD66606-1029) 'shape at weight one and compare the deformed surfaces, one shape at a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:02:27Z (RFD66606-1029) 'time, or a destroyed expression ships looking fine.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1029  1 LINE
 Text:Written

